<p>Angostura bitters is a concentrated bitters (aka a herbal alcoholic preparation) based on gentian (a plant with a bitter root), herbs, and spices.</p>
<p>It’s produced by the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House_of_Angostura" rel="noopener">House of Angostura</a> in Trinidad and Tobago and is called Angostura as it was created in the town of Angostura in Venezuela.</p>
<p>Angostura Bitters are typically used for flavouring drinks, and the House of Angostura also makes orange bitters.</p>
